      "side": 1,
      "message": "The frustrating part is, RemovePointerLets makes the right IR:\n\n```\n%f \u003d func():i32 {\n  $B1: {\n    ret 0i\n  }\n}\n%g \u003d func():i32 {\n  $B2: {\n    ret 0i\n  }\n}\n%fpp \u003d func():void {\n  $B3: {\n    %arr:ptr\u003cfunction, array\u003ci32, 4\u003e, read_write\u003e \u003d var\n    %5:i32 \u003d call %f\n    %6:ptr\u003cfunction, i32, read_write\u003e \u003d access %arr, %5\n    %7:i32 \u003d call %g\n    %y:i32 \u003d let %7\n    %9:i32 \u003d load %6\n    %x:i32 \u003d let %9\n    ret\n  }\n}\n```\n\nBut, because the backends inline all `access` it goes wonky. I wonder if `ValueToLet` can be made smarter to deal with access indices in a nicer fashion.",
